00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:20.020
The planning areas together cover approximately 127,000 hectares of ecosystems and wilderness.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:32.560
No new regulatory thresholds or amended standards were released with the announcement, but the plans will establish management objectives that can constrain future land use and remediation activities.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:45.240
Consultants conducting phase 1 and phase 2 ESAs or preparing risk assessments near these blocks should confirm whether proposed investigation or remediation works intersect with the planning boundaries.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.340
Next steps include release of detailed planning terms of reference.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:56.080
Practitioners should request copies directly from the Ministry to identify any new information requirements.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:03.940
Three separate planning processes have started that will define objectives for roughly 127,000 hectares.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:12.660
The resulting plans may impose new constraints on industrial activity and site remediation within or adjacent to the planning areas.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.920
No comment deadline has been published. BC Hydro is distributing free smart thermostats.

