Climate-driven permafrost law combined with increased rainfall is generating sulfuric acid in rivers and lakes across Arctic Canada.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:58.660
Resulting pH declines can mobilize metals and alter background water quality conditions used in northern site assessments.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.420
The reporting appears in the TAE.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:08.180
The article carries the title, Rusting Rivers, alarm grows over rising acid in Arctic waters.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:16.780
Published online July 7, 2026, marine mammals are extending dive times in response to changing prey distributions.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.940
The finding appears in nature climate change.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.020
The finding has limited direct application to contaminated dash sites work.

